UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 606-10-25-27, when total estimated costs exceed the contract price, the entire expected loss must be recognized immediately in the current period regardless of percentage of completion. This is the onerous contract provision.
Wrong (B): Proportional recognition applies to profitable contracts; losses on onerous contracts are recognized in full when identified.
Wrong (C): Deferring loss recognition would understate liabilities and overstate income, violating the conservatism principle embedded in the standard.
Wrong (D): Renegotiation is a business decision, not an accounting treatment; the loss must be recognized based on current estimates.$EXPL$
